Subject: [PATCH 3/4] sr-aef: make glyph names unique as fontTools does

A post table may give two glyphs the same name (Sansation Light Italic names
two glyphs ffi). The uncompiled features then named both alike, and a
compiler could neither tell them apart nor, given a source with the
duplicate, build at all. unique_glyph_names() gives a name already taken the
first free suffix of .1, .2, ..., as fontTools does; it is public so that a
converter names the glyphs as the features do.

Assisted by an AI agent (Claude Opus 5.5)
